4. DORMANCY AND AUTOMATIC RELICENSING

The Author intends this project to survive the Author. This section converts the
license automatically if the Author becomes inactive or unreachable.

4.1 Trigger. This section is triggered when either condition is met:

    (a) No commit authored by the Author has been pushed to the Canonical
        Repository for 365 consecutive days; or

    (b) The Author has failed to respond within 90 days to a good-faith contact
        attempt made through BOTH of the following: a message to the Discord
        account named in section 1.2, and a public issue opened in the Canonical
        Repository.

4.2 Notice and cure. Before relying on this section, You must open a public
    issue in the Canonical Repository titled "Dormancy notice" stating which
    condition You believe is met, and wait 30 days. If the Author responds in
    that window, or pushes a commit in that window, this section is not
    triggered and both clocks reset.

4.3 Effect. Once triggered and the cure period has passed without response, this
    license converts irrevocably, for everyone, to the MIT License, with the
    copyright notice "Copyright (c) 2026 Leclowndu93150 and contributors". From
    that moment sections 3.1 through 3.3 no longer apply.

4.4 Scope. The conversion in section 4.3 applies only to material the Author is
    entitled to license. It does not and cannot grant rights in the material
    described in section 5.

4.5 Reset. Any commit pushed by the Author to the Canonical Repository restarts
    the period in section 4.1(a).


